# Keep line endings consistent no matter what writes into this repository -
# Windows, macOS, Linux, a web upload, or a tool acting on your behalf.
#
# text=auto tells Git to store every text file with LF endings in the
# repository, and to check it out with the platform's native endings
# (CRLF on Windows). Binary files are detected automatically and left alone.
#
# Without this, a file written with LF endings looks like every single line
# changed, which buries real edits in noise.

* text=auto
